        {
          "id": "pub-el-b1-0017",
          "left": "48px",
          "top": "586px",
          "width": "442px",
          "height": "245px",
          "transform": "none",
          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:12px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.58; text-align:left; word-wrap:break-word; \"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><span style=\"float:left; font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:44px; line-height:0.86; font-weight:800; color:#0f5c57; padding-right:8px; padding-top:4px;\">M</span>ore than 140 neighborhood volunteers gathered over six weekends this autumn to replace aging timber crossings along the 3.4-kilometer Mill Creek Greenway. Funded jointly by club membership dues and our municipal green-space grant, the new cedar bridges improve safe accessibility for strollers, runners, and seniors year-round.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Alongside the bridge work, the Horticulture Guild seeded 18,000 square feet of drought-tolerant prairie grasses to stabilize creek banks and support local pollinators throughout spring.</p><p style=\"margin:0;\">A formal ribbon-cutting walk departs from the Pavilion at 10:00 AM next Saturday, followed by warm cider and community sign-ups for the 2027 maintenance roster.</p></div>",
          "imgSrc": "",
          "clipPath": "",
          "bg": "",
          "cropMode": false,
          "imgStyle": {},
          "scaleX": "1",
          "scaleY": "1",
