          "width": "212px",
          "height": "430px",
          "transform": "none",
          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:11.2px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.52; text-align:left; word-wrap:break-word; \"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Before the first hard frost arrives in late November, spread two inches of shredded leaf compost over perennial beds. Avoid cutting hollow stems back until spring so beneficial solitary bees keep their winter shelters.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Community plot renewals open Dec 1. Raised Bed Zone C receives fresh drip-irrigation lines before April planting.</p><p style=\"margin:0;\"><strong style=\"color:#0f5c57;\">Seed Swap Drawer:</strong> Clean heirloom envelopes are stocked inside the greenhouse porch daily from dawn to dusk.</p></div>",
          "imgSrc": "",
          "clipPath": "",
