          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:11.2px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.52; text-align:left; word-wrap:break-word; \"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Daylight savings means darker evening commutes along Birch and Elm corridors. Homeowners are encouraged to test motion porch timers and trim hedges blocking corner visibility.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Crosswalk Flashing Beacons:</strong> Thanks to parent petitions, high-visibility pedestrian beacons went live outside Oakridge Elementary this week.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Block captains meet first Mondays at 6:30 PM to share safety updates and welcome new households moving onto our streets.</p><div style=\"background:#f3ede2; border-left:3px solid #c26d1f; padding:10px; font-size:10.8px; line-height:1.45;\"><strong>Winter Salt Bins:</strong> Yellow grit bins are refilled at all steep hill intersections. Please bring a small scoop for sidewalks.</div></div>",
