          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:11px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.45; text-align:left; word-wrap:break-word; \"><div style=\"font-size:10px; font-weight:700; color:#c26d1f; letter-spacing:1.2px; margin-bottom:4px;\">BAKER'S CORNER</div><div style=\"font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:18px; font-weight:800; color:#0f5c57; margin-bottom:10px;\">Spiced Apple &amp; Oat Galette</div><div style=\"font-size:10.8px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.48;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;\"><em>Contributed by Hannah Ortiz for the Harvest Potluck table:</em></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Crust:</strong> Whisk 1.5 cups flour, 2 tbsp rolled oats, pinch sea salt, and cut in 10 tbsp cold butter until pea-sized. Add 4 tbsp ice water; chill 30 min.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;\"><strong>Filling:</strong> Toss 4 sliced Honeycrisp apples with 3 tbsp brown sugar, 1 tsp cinnamon, 1 tsp lemon juice, and 1 tbsp cornstarch.</p><p style=\"margin:0;\">Roll circle, pile fruit in center, fold edges inward, brush cream, and bake at 400F for 38 minutes until golden.</p></div></div>",
